('LOC_GREATPERSON_ADD_SUPER_SPECIALIST_MERCHANT', 'Add Great Merchant to city. Grants +6 [ICON_Gold] Gold, +1 [ICON_Food]Food, and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Merchant Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_GREATPERSON_ADD_SUPER_SPECIALIST_SCIENTIST', 'Add Great Sage to city. Grants +6 [ICON_Science]Science, +1 [ICON_Production]Production, and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Sage Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_GREATPERSON_ADD_SUPER_SPECIALIST_ARTIST', 'Add Great Bard to city. Grants +12 [ICON_Culture]Culture, +3 [ICON_Gold]Gold, and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Bard Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_GREATPERSON_ADD_SUPER_SPECIALIST_ENGINEER', 'Add Great Engineer to city. Grants +3 [ICON_Science]Science, +3 [ICON_Production]Production, and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Engineer Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_GREATPERSON_ADD_SUPER_SPECIALIST_PROPHET', 'Add Great Prophet to city. Grants +5 [ICON_Gold]Gold, +2 [ICON_Production]Production, and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Prophet Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_CITIES_9_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_1', 'Specialists are alternative assignments for [ICON_Citizen] Citizens, which involve working a district tile instead of a normal tile. As a general rule, specialists are a good way to get yields otherwise hard to find on normal tiles, but the city needs a solid support base of [ICON_Food] Food to support them in the long term. Specialists are also particularly useful when a city grows large later in the game, and has more [ICON_Citizen] Population than there are normal tiles to work. There are different types of specialists, each with different effects. All specialist types except the generic [ICON_Citizen] Citizen have a limit on how many assignments there can be in a city.Normally, you can slot additional specialists from buildings in the district associated with that specialist type, but some Wonders or policies allow more. Check the building''s page to see if they add to the district additional [ICON_Citizen] Citizens yields.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_CITIES_9_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_2', 'Sages work in the Campus and provide +3 [ICON_Science]Science and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Sage Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_CITIES_9_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_3', 'Priests work in the Holy Site and provide +1 [ICON_Gold]Gold, +1 [ICON_Production]Production and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Prophet Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_CITIES_9_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_6', 'Merchants work in the Commercial Hub and provide +3 [ICON_Gold] Gold and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Merchant Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_CITIES_9_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_7', 'Engineers work in the Industrial Zone and provide +2 [ICON_Production] Production  and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Engineer Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_CITIES_9_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_8', 'Bards work in the Theater Square and provide +4 [ICON_Culture] Culture, +1 [ICON_Science]Science and +1 [ICON_GreatPerson]Great Bard Point per turn.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_FAITH_4_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_1', '[ICON_GreatProphet] Great Prophets can be used to upgrade the Altar of the Luonnotar, leading towards a Religious victory, if you have the Tech/Civic unlock. They can also be used to make Holy City Wonders, if you have a city that founded that Religion. They can also be placed as a Super Specialist.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_GOVT_4_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_5', 'State Religion: This Policy determines which religion your government works with. This allows you to build the unique units, special abilities and heroes of the religion.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_COMMERCE_CHAPTER_CONTENT_TITLE', 'Commerce', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_COMMERCE_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_1', 'In Civilization IV, [ICON_Science]Science, [ICON_Culture]Culture and [ICON_Gold]Gold were earned most oftenly from [ICON_Faith]Commerce. [ICON_Faith]Commerce was a yield that could be adjusted in the proportions of [ICON_Science]Science, and later [ICON_Culture]Culture, that could be converted from this [ICON_Faith]Commerce, the rest going to [ICON_Gold]Gold.', 'en_US'),
('LOC_PEDIA_CONCEPTS_PAGE_COMMERCE_CHAPTER_CONTENT_PARA_2', 'In VI, this has been approximated by using the unused [ICON_Faith]Faith yield, as Commerce. By default, your cities will convert this yield into a third [ICON_Science]Science, a third [ICON_Culture]Culture, and a third [ICON_Gold]Gold. In future, this will be adjustable with sliders in the UI, like Soren Johnson intended all those years ago.', 'en_US'),
